{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 3]], "date-time": "2026-06-03T17:08:59Z", "timestamp": 1780506539973, "version": "3.54.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2020, 2, 3]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2020, 2, 3]], "date-time": "2020-02-03T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1580688000000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": [], "abstract": "<jats:p>Lithium-ion batteries have become the mainstream energy storage solution\nfor many applications, such as electric vehicles and smart grids.\nHowever, various faults in a lithium-ion battery system (LIBS) can\npotentially cause performance degradation and severe safety issues.\nDeveloping advanced fault diagnosis technologies is becoming\nincreasingly critical for the safe operation of LIBS. This paper\nprovides a comprehensive review of fault mechanisms, fault features, and\nfault diagnosis of various faults in LIBS, including internal battery\nfaults, sensor faults, and actuator faults. Future trends in the\ndevelopment of fault diagnosis technologies for a safer battery system\nare presented and discussed.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.11777448.v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2020, 2, 3]], "date-time": "2020-02-03T04:15:49Z", "timestamp": 1580703349000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 5, "title": ["Advanced Fault Diagnosis for Lithium-Ion Battery Systems"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"given": "Xiaosong", "family": "Hu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Chongqing University"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Kai", "family": "Zhang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Kailong", "fa